WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.020
European Union regulations&nbsp;
which bans over 1600 chemicals

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:07.320
This whole idea that EU products are&nbsp;
safer because they ban more stuff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.900
really bothers me because it's just not true

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:12.960
unsafe products are banned in&nbsp;
the US including if they have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:15.960
unsafe levels of anything it's called adulterated

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:19.500
The US law has a list of 11&nbsp;
ingredient categories that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:23.640
are explicitly banned but this isn't meant&nbsp;
to be everything these are just examples

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.580
The EU's list also isn't meant to&nbsp;
include everything they've just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:29.760
got more examples and their list&nbsp;
includes a whole bunch of things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:33.960
that no one would ever intentionally put&nbsp;
into cosmetics like radioactive substances

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:37.860
There are lots of examples of the FDA&nbsp;
saying that unsafe products are illegal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:41.700
because they contain unsafe levels of&nbsp;
something that wasn't on that list of 11

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:45.300
so for example these products had&nbsp;
harmful levels of bacteria or mould

